# Manual API checks. Run the API with: dotnet run --project src/TaskManagement.Api --launch-profile http
# In VS Code, use the REST Client extension; Visual Studio and Rider support .http files natively.

@host = http://localhost:5062
# Paste an id returned by "Create a task" here before running the requests below it.
@taskId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### List all tasks
GET {{host}}/api/tasks
Accept: application/json

### Filter by status and priority
GET {{host}}/api/tasks?status=ToDo&priority=High
Accept: application/json

### Create a task (201 + Location header)
POST {{host}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare sprint review",
  "description": "Collect demo items and metrics.",
  "priority": "High",
  "assignedTo": "Jordan"
}

### Create with invalid data (400: missing title)
POST {{host}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "priority": "Urgent"
}

### Get task details
GET {{host}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}
Accept: application/json

### Update a task (full replacement of editable fields)
PUT {{host}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare and rehearse sprint review",
  "description": "Collect demo items, metrics and rehearse once.",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "assignedTo": "Jordan"
}

### Change status
PATCH {{host}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "InProgress"
}

### Delete a task (204)
DELETE {{host}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}

### Nonexistent task (404)
GET {{host}}/api/tasks/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
